  "details": "A significant issue exists with users giving random people their VRChat account to upload an avatar. A way a user could send an avatar upload to another user account and get an email about it or a notification on the website saying a user is requesting to upload an avatar to their account. The user then could accept or decline the upload. There could also be a system like 2FA where a user could give another user a code that lasts 24 hours, which they could provide to the user if they want to upload the avatar and follow the steps I mentioned earlier. Alongside that, there could be a disclaimer stating that the user accepting the avatar upload is responsible for the avatar being uploaded to their account and that VRChat recommends checking their avatar in a private lobby before taking it out in public. This new proposed function would prevent users from giving out their private info and having their accounts deleted or getting wrongfully banned for unauthorized account access.",
